<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edward Braddock</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1695">1695</a>–<a href="/years/1755">1755</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edward Braddock was a British general sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> in 1755 as commander-in-chief at the start of the French and Indian War. Leading an expedition against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-duquesne">Fort Duquesne</a>, he was defeated and mortally wounded by French and Native forces at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-monongahela">Battle of the Monongahela</a> on 9 July 1755. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a>, one of his aides, helped organise the retreat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edward-braddock.jpg" alt="Edward Braddock" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Sartain · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edward_Braddock_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
